                    },
                    "message": "Is there a reason u r not doing this inline at line#89 but creating a new var ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/leakdetector/LeakDetectionManager.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "So at that point we have a client which has a proxy which has a reference to a string (since `Preserved == false` by default)\n\nSince the temporary object is alive until the end of the full expression, and\n`.properties()` already creates the D-Bus message with the path copied into it,\nwe should be safe to use a temporary object as you suggested!\n\nHowever the API does not support temporary objects\n```\n/* Convert a non-Path instance to a Path instance. */\nauto path(auto& p) const noexcept\n          requires(!P)\n{\n     return client<S, true, Preserved, Types...>(ctx, proxy.path(p)); \n}\n```\n\nsince temporary objects do not bind to non-const reference.\n\n\nLet me know if the explanation is lacking or i missed anything.\n\nLong term the client and proxy should probably get an overload that directly support object_path."
                }
            ],
